    {
      "ID": "cc5wu",
      "Author": "template",
      "Timestamp": "2026-08-05T14:42:00.532893-07:00",
      "Text": "[Q] Resolve ambiguity: [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: is a full glamour \"reading mode\" toggle (`v`, reflowed, anchors degrade to section badges) worth shipping in v1, or defer until in-place styling proves insufficient?]",
      "Type": "Q",
      "Line": 26,
      "SectionID": "s4",
      "SectionPath": "Review-First TUI Redesign \u003e Proposed Design",
      "Anchor": {
        "selected_text": "**In-place typography, no reflow (G1).** Style body prose where it sits: bold/italic/code spans rendered styled with their syntax glyphs dimmed, list bullets and blockquote bars colored, headings as today. Every source line stays exactly one wrapped display unit (`↪` continuations share the line number), so gutter markers and anchors remain truthful. [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: is a full glamour \"reading mode\" toggle (`v`, reflowed, anchors degrade to section badges) worth shipping in v1, or defer until in-place styling proves insufficient?]"
      },
      "AnchorConfidence": "section-level",
      "Resolved": true,
      "Blocking": true,
